cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  IDKMesh: verified swarm engineering for humans, AI agents, and
  heterogeneous compute
message: >-
  If you use IDKMesh, or build on its Work Unit, ResultManifest, EvaluatorPlan,
  or VerificationResult contracts, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohsen
    family-names: Seyedkazemi Ardebili
    email: mohsen.seyedkazemi@gmail.com
    alias: MSKazemi
repository-code: https://github.com/MSKazemi/idkmesh
url: https://mskazemi.com/idkmesh/
abstract: >-
  IDKMesh is an open-source research laboratory studying whether a large open
  community of humans and AI agents can discover goals, decompose work, execute
  bounded tasks, verify results independently, and maintain complex systems
  better than isolated developers or agents can. It provides versioned task and
  evidence contracts that separate worker claims from independent verification
  from integration authority, together with simulation and benchmark
  infrastructure for testing those questions empirically. The repository is an
  executable research foundation; implemented infrastructure is evidence of the
  capability to run experiments, not evidence that the research hypotheses are
  true.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent orchestration
  - collective intelligence
  - software verification
  - distributed systems
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
